      "hints": [
        "Substitute $y = 5x - 10$ into $(x-5)^2 + (y-2)^2 = 13$ to get $26x^2 - 130x + 156 = 0$.",
        "Factorise $x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0$ to find $x = 2$ and $x = 3$.",
        "Find coordinates $(2, 0)$ and $(3, 5)$, then compute distance $AB = \\sqrt{26}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $y = 5x - 10$ into the circle equation $(x - 5)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = 13$:\n$$(x - 5)^2 + (5x - 12)^2 = 13$$",
        "Expand and simplify into a quadratic equation in $x$:\n$$(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (25x^2 - 120x + 144) = 13 \\implies 26x^2 - 130x + 156 = 0$$",
        "Divide by $26$ and factorise to solve for $x$:\n$$x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 \\implies (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0 \\implies x = 2, \\quad x = 3$$",
        "Find the corresponding $y$-coordinates of intersection points $A$ and $B$:\n$$\\text{At } x = 2:\\quad y = 5(2) - 10 = 0 \\implies A(2, 0)$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 3:\\quad y = 5(3) - 10 = 5 \\implies B(3, 5)$$",
        "Apply the distance formula between $A(2, 0)$ and $B(3, 5)$ to find the exact chord length:\n$$AB = \\sqrt{(3 - 2)^2 + (5 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{1^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{26}$$"
